<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28206" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mătĭus</span></b> , a,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a
				Roman</i> gens. So, Cn. Matius, <i>a poet and
				translator of the Iliad</i>, <i><span class="en">Gell. 6, 6,
				5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 14,
			14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 7, 5, § 96</span></i>
			Müll.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perh. the same with C. Matius,</span>”
				<i>a friend of Cæsar and Cicero</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 6, 12, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">7, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 12, 2,
				6, § 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 12,
				4, 2 al.</span></i>—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mătĭā-nus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to a Matius, Matian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mala,</span>”
				<i>a kind of apple</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					5, 10, 19</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">12, 47, 5</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Suet. Dom. 21</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">poma,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Front. de Fer. Als. 3</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Minutal,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Apic. 4,
					3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
